## THE 5 VITAL RULES (Always In Context)

These rules must NEVER leave your active context:

### VITAL 1: DOCUMENT EVERYTHING AS YOU GO
> "DOCUMENT everything little thing along the way, don't ever STOP documenting, no matter what you do."

- Document DURING work, not after
- Every finding → immediate documentation
- No batching, no "I'll add this later"

### VITAL 2: 10X VERIFICATION
> "Everything you do, you gotta do it 10X. Time is not important."

- Every phase: 10 iterations
- Every task: scaled 10x verification
- Each iteration must be DOCUMENTED (prove you did it)

### VITAL 3: ONE THING AT A TIME
> "Even when working autonomously you gotta be EXTREMELY compliant with methodology."

- One file at a time
- One section at a time
- Complete and document before moving on

### VITAL 4: EXHAUSTIVE THOROUGHNESS
> "Be exhaustive with extreme thoroughness and accuracy all the time."

- No superficial answers
- No "it looks fine"
- Specific, detailed, verified

### VITAL 5: UNIVERSAL APPLICATION
> "Anything I tell them to do, it AUTOMATICALLY needs to be done by METHODOLOGY, even if it seems something unimportant."

- NO task is "too small" for methodology
- NO task is "too simple" for documentation
- NO task is exempt from 10x

