## AUTONOMOUS WORK ≠ SKIP METHODOLOGY

**CRITICAL CLARIFICATION:**

Rule 2.1 allows autonomous work for research and adding information.
This does NOT mean you skip methodology during autonomous work.

```
AUTONOMOUS MEANS:
✅ You can proceed without asking PO permission
✅ You can research and add findings freely

AUTONOMOUS DOES NOT MEAN:
❌ Skip documentation
❌ Skip 10x verification
❌ Skip one-thing-at-a-time
❌ Work faster by cutting corners

AUTONOMOUS + METHODOLOGY = CORRECT
AUTONOMOUS - METHODOLOGY = FAILURE
```

---

## WHAT "DONE" MEANS

A task is NOT done when you finish working on it.
A task is DONE when:

| Requirement | Check |
|-------------|-------|
| Work completed | □ |
| 10x verification COMPLETED and DOCUMENTED | □ |
| Every finding documented | □ |
| WHY documented for every addition | □ |
| Cross-references verified | □ |
| No contradictions introduced | □ |
| PO could audit and find ZERO gaps | □ |

**If ANY box is unchecked → Task is NOT done.**

